## Decision 0002: replace subject-only deduplication

This record supersedes [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).
The accepted historical record is preserved unchanged. The active
[triage runbook](/kb/triage/dedupe) now requires evidence of the same cause before merging.

<Callout kind="warn">
The old #4471 narrative says “one issue, one fix queued.” Its own computed evidence shows
two distinct product problems. The later engineering update below gives a separate outcome for each problem.
It does not provide independent deployment or product-test evidence.
</Callout>

<DeskOutcome />

## Scope and evidence

This review was performed on 31 October 2026 against the support kb export dated
4 October 2026. It describes a snapshot, not today's live support queue.
The reports and tenant files are preserved unchanged. Tables and charts run the supplied
logic in `causes.ts`, `locales.ts` and the kb components at render time.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Problem A: month-first shared parser in day-first tenants

The shared parser interprets dates as month/day while the tenant writes day/month.
For example, Harbour Dental's app report R-41200 describes 7 April becoming 4 July;
Lantern Row's app report R-41203 describes 2 December becoming 12 February.
The parser cohort covers app and email reports in day-first tenants, and form reports
where the form does not introduce the booking-v3 hint defect.

**Engineering ticket:** [GitHub #1 — parser](https://github.com/lpietrzak83/megadev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
The source-of-truth count and scope appear in the computed table above.
The cohort includes the unresolved observations listed below; it does not establish
a parser root cause for every body. Preserve those caveats during follow-up.

**Original verification proposal (not executed; engineering notice governs disposition):** Test an unambiguous tenant date convention and an ambiguous numeric example
such as `07/04/2026`: the intended 7 April must remain 7 April in the invite.
Test app, email and applicable booking-v2 form paths. The proposed parser and hint checks address different input paths.

## Problem B: booking-v3 prints the wrong date-format hint

Booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` for tenants whose form interprets dates in the tenant's day-first
convention. Following the hint supplies month first to a day-first form.
This is a separate UI/input contract defect, even when its symptoms resemble the parser defect.
The affected form reports come from Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.
App/email reports at those same tenants still belong in the parser cohort.

Examples: Copper Studio form report R-41230 and Alder Physio form report R-41241.
Both were merged into #4471, but neither is resolved merely by changing the shared parser.

**Engineering ticket:** [GitHub #2 — booking-v3 hint](https://github.com/lpietrzak83/megadev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
**Original verification proposal (superseded by form retirement):** Check that displayed guidance, accepted input and resulting booking agree for each tenant locale.
For a day-first tenant, entering 6 January according to the displayed guidance must preserve 6 January.
Check both booking-v3 and booking-v2, with browser locale differing from the tenant locale.

